  {
   "turn": 8,
   "response_text": "Perfect. This confirms the issue. The `eval_subset_fraction` is set to 0.5, which means the reported validation accuracy is computed on only the most confident 50% of the validation set, not the full validation set. This is clearly wrong for measuring model performance honestly.\n\nThe healthy runs should have either:\n1. `eval_subset_fraction` set to `null` or `1.0` (to report on the full validation set), or\n2. This configuration removed entirely (which defaults to reporting on the full set)\n\nLet me gather the evidence and submit my diagnosis:",
